Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define the initial number step, the final one, and the \
interval between each step that is going to be imported.
The Table FNames contained the names of the output files up to the location \
in your laptop.
You can choose \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]constrained\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]bulk\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]boundary\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] depending which kind of \
file you want to read.
Don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t forget the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]_\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] after.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.924594575349163*^9, 
  3.924594720815542*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"11e42d42-cd3a-4d74-bfcf-\
1d8db2aafacc"],

