Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s plot! The variable t specify the time step you have \
acquired in input. Inside the ListContourPlot function, there is the previous \
table GridSF, and we need to Flatten it. In the title of the plot should \
compare the time of the screenshot you are visualising (if something doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t feel right, check that you define the correct dt or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]each\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] parameter in the first \
cell of this notebook). In alternative, you can substitute ListPlot3D or \
ListDensityPlot to ListContourPlot to have a different visualization of the \
plot. Commented there is also the PlotRange option that can be used to zoom \
in a specific region.\
\>", "Text",
